00:00:02.389 --> 00:00:04.130 align:start position:0%
Super Smash Brothers ultimate may look  similar to the Wii U version but there  are a lot of changes under the hood if  you want to be at the top of your game  you might want to familiarize yourself  with some of these changes and  strategies we're gonna start with the  basic tactics and end on the advanced  ones the whole point of Super Smash  Brothers is to knock your opponent off  the stage before he or she knocks you  off the stage unfortunately there will  be times when you get knocked off first  and will have to recover most characters  have a jump and then a double jump as  well as a special move that will get  them a little bit more distance however  this special move varies from character  to character for example link can use a  sword to spin like a helicopter and Ness  can use his PK Thunder to send them  flying in any direction some characters  might have a really good stage recovery  like Kirby and Pitt while others such as  in sinner or or Little Mac have terrible  recoveries some characters even have  multiple specials that can be used for  stage recovery Ike for example can use  the side special to recover a lot of  horizontal ground as you play around  with different characters make sure you  get a feeling for how each of their  recovery Styles work  [Music]  for most characters smash texts are  their most powerful moves smash attacks  can be performed by pressing a and  inputting a direction at the same time  alternatively you can also use the right  stick to use these moves you can charge  these attacks to inflict higher damage  but be careful though most of these  moves have a lengthy recovery time and  are pretty easy to dodge  the final smashes have all been  rebalanced thank goodness there are no  longer any final smash attacks that  allow you to transform into a  super-powered character for a limited  time and instead most of the final  smashes require you to be within arm's  length of your victim you really want to  wait for the right time before using  mamie fighters like Ike kromm Marth king  K rool and Peach are equipped with a  countermove  if you time the special maneuver  correctly you will counter another  fighters attack and deal a nice bit of  damage back at them practice this enough  and you'll find that successfully  countering an opponent is also one of  the most satisfying experiences in the  game  once again you can spot dodge roll and  air dodge however they work a little bit  differently in ultimate for starters you  can now perform directional air dodges  by inputting a direction with the dodge  you can even shift momentum with the  directional air dodge however there is a  lengthy recovery window so keep that in  mind you can perform a roll by inputting  right or left with the shield button  like in previous games this is a good  way to get on the other side of your  opponent encounter however if you roll  too many times in succession your  recovery will take longer and if your  timing is off this could leave you open  to a devastating smash attack spot  dodging occurs when you input down in a  shield and this grants you a few frames  of invulnerability these can be pretty  tricky at a time however if you  successfully spot dodge you can easily  counter your opponent from what we can  tell spot dodging multiple times in a  row doesn't seem to have any negative  effects learning how the dodge correctly  is key to Super Smash Brothers and it's  no different in ultimate learning which  dodge to use and when takes a lot of  practice but it can give you a  significant advantage against tougher  opponents  performing short hop attacks in previous  smash games always required a bit of  dexterity luckily in ultimate you can  actually press attack and jump at the  same time to do a short hop attack this  is useful because you can use it to  change up your standard - attack and  because it's a short hop you won't spend  that much time in the air as you build  up damage you might notice that your  character will start to smoke and flash  red this means that they are enraged  while enraged you deal more damage and  hit your opponent's harder rage can also  be used to close the damage gap between  you and your opponent if one exists for  the most part shielding works similarly  to pass smash games while on the ground  you can throw up your shield and it will  protect you from all incoming attacks  but over time your shield will shrink  and eventually it will break and when it  does break you won't be able to attack  or move for a period of time one big  change with shielding however is how  perfect shielding works if you drop your  shield right before an attack connects  with you the attacker will be stunned  momentarily the duration of the stun  differs depending on the strength of the  attack and if done correctly you can  follow up your opponent's attack with  one of your own getting the timing down  this is pretty tough so we'd recommend  jumping into training like right here  and set the CPU behavior to side smash  if you perform a perfect shield  correctly your character will flash  so those are just a few tips for super  smash brothers ultimate if you want to  get really good at ultimate we'd  recommend turning off items and playing  on battlefield or final destination map  variants this will allow you to focus  solely on the mechanics instead of  chasing down the best items or dodging  stage obstacles if you have more  techniques that you want to share feel  free to drop them in the comments below  and thanks for watching  [Music]
 

